From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 20:18:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07197/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-16: 5x search
 budget does not rescue the 5699-15 wall -- not a tunable-parameter fix

Added a DEV-ONLY CARNOT_ARC_PLAN_MAX_NODES env override to _call_plan_in_model
(unset in production, byte-identical default; guarded by a
_planner_accepts_max_nodes signature check matching the existing
goal_energy/diagnostics pattern), then re-ran sp80 budget=250 with
CARNOT_ARC_PLAN_MAX_NODES=100000 -- 5x plan_in_model's 20000-node default.

Result: termination_reason is still "max_nodes_reached" at nodes_expanded
~100000 for both arms independently (100015/100001), planned=false. 5x more
search budget did not find a plan against the tier-1 CNN-dynamics-prior
engine, ruling out the tunable-parameter-fix hypothesis REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-15
raised. Combined with 5699-15 (the goal predicate is real,
is_level_complete_was_none=false), the sharper remaining explanation is that
the induced model's multi-step rollout does not represent a discoverable
path to its own goal predicate -- either locally-accurate-but-not-globally-
coherent dynamics, or a dynamics/goal self-consistency gap. Distinguishing
those would require inspecting the model's own predicted rollout directly, a
materially deeper investigation than the last three REQs -- flagged as a
natural checkpoint rather than continuing open-endedly on one n=1 game.

